1
00:00:01,376 --> 00:00:03,671
HEY, YOU'RE NOT GOING
TO BELIEVE THIS.

2
00:00:03,671 --> 00:00:06,674
I MADE UP A JOKE
AND SENT IT IN TO PLAYBOY.

3
00:00:06,674 --> 00:00:10,135
THEY PRINTED IT.

4
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:12,095
I DIDN'T KNOW PLAYBOY
PRINTS JOKES.

5
00:00:12,095 --> 00:00:14,348
YEAH, THEY PRINT JOKES,
UH, INTERVIEWS

6
00:00:14,348 --> 00:00:15,808
HARD-HITTING JOURNALISM.

7
00:00:15,808 --> 00:00:17,392
IT'S NOT JUST
ABOUT THE PICTURES.

8
00:00:17,392 --> 00:00:18,686
IT DIDN'T
WORK ON MOM.

9
00:00:18,686 --> 00:00:21,313
IT'S NOT GOING
TO WORK ON US.

10
00:00:21,313 --> 00:00:22,356
HERE, CHECK IT OUT.

11
00:00:22,356 --> 00:00:23,691
IT'S THE FIRST ONE, TOO.

12
00:00:25,024 --> 00:00:26,902
RIGHT THERE.

13
00:00:26,902 --> 00:00:29,029
( all chuckling )

14
00:00:29,029 --> 00:00:30,364
THAT IS FUNNY.

15
00:00:30,364 --> 00:00:32,616
IT WAS ALSO FUNNY
WHEN I MADE IT UP.

16
00:00:34,743 --> 00:00:36,954
WHAT?
I MADE THAT JOKE UP.

17
00:00:36,954 --> 00:00:38,873
UH, OH, NO, YOU DIDN'T. I DID.

18
00:00:38,873 --> 00:00:40,332
UH-UH-OH, YES, I DID.

19
00:00:40,332 --> 00:00:42,125
I TOLD IT TO DAN AT WORK
AND HE SAID IT WAS

20
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:43,669
THE FUNNIEST JOKE
HE'D EVER HEARD.

21
00:00:43,669 --> 00:00:45,838
HEY, TELL DAN "THANKS."

22
00:00:50,175 --> 00:00:51,760
WHAT?

23
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,762
I'M SORRY. I WAS JUST READING
THE JOKE BELOW IT.

24
00:00:53,762 --> 00:00:55,305
THAT ONE IS FUNNY.

25
00:00:57,850 --> 00:01:01,353
MONICA, YOU REMEMBER ME
TELLING YOU THAT JOKE, RIGHT?

26
00:01:01,353 --> 00:01:02,354
NO.

27
00:01:02,354 --> 00:01:03,522
SERIOUSLY?

28
00:01:03,522 --> 00:01:05,357
WELL, YOU TELL
A LOT OF JOKES.

29
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:08,903
LOOK, CHANDLER,
IT'S MY JOKE.

30
00:01:08,903 --> 00:01:10,988
HEY, IF IT MAKES YOU
FEEL ANY BETTER

31
00:01:10,988 --> 00:01:13,323
THEY DON'T PRINT THE NAME,
SO IT DOESN'T REALLY MATTER

32
00:01:13,323 --> 00:01:14,575
WHO GETS CREDIT, RIGHT?

33
00:01:14,575 --> 00:01:15,784
I GUESS NOT.

34
00:01:15,784 --> 00:01:17,244
HEY, GUYS.

35
00:01:17,244 --> 00:01:18,996
HEY, JOEY!
PLAYBOY PRINTED MY JOKE!

36
00:01:18,996 --> 00:01:20,873
NO! NO! IT'S MY MINE!
IT'S MY JOKE!

37
00:01:20,873 --> 00:01:22,123
YOU CAN CALL THEM.
THEY'LL TELL YOU.

38
00:01:22,123 --> 00:01:23,124
IT'S MY JOKE.
IT'S MY JOKE!

39
00:01:23,124 --> 00:01:25,002
WHOA! WHOA! WHOA!

40
00:01:25,002 --> 00:01:26,921
JOKES?

41
00:01:26,921 --> 00:01:29,715
YOU GUYS KNOW THEY HAVE
NAKED CHICKS IN THERE, RIGHT?

42
00:01:36,889 --> 00:01:41,936
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

43
00:01:41,936 --> 00:01:44,103
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

44
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:46,941
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

45
00:01:46,941 --> 00:01:51,445
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

46
00:01:51,445 --> 00:01:54,073
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN
YOUR DAY, YOUR WEEK ♪

47
00:01:54,073 --> 00:01:56,617
♪ YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

48
00:01:56,617 --> 00:02:00,412
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

49
00:02:00,412 --> 00:02:03,874
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

50
00:02:11,673 --> 00:02:14,760
DUDE, DUDE, YOU HAVE GOT TO
TURN ON BEHIND THE MUSIC.

51
00:02:14,760 --> 00:02:16,762
THE BAND HEART IS HAVING
A REALLY TOUGH TIME

52
00:02:16,762 --> 00:02:18,513
AND I THINK THEY
MAY BREAK UP.

53
00:02:18,513 --> 00:02:20,348
HEY, LET'S GO WATCH
THAT AT YOUR PLACE.

54
00:02:20,348 --> 00:02:22,183
NO, NO, NO, MONICA'S WATCHING
SOME COOKING SHOW.

55
00:02:22,183 --> 00:02:24,979
COME ON, I DON'T WANT TO MISS
WHEN THEY WERE SKINNY.

56
00:02:24,979 --> 00:02:26,187
UH, HEY-HEY,
CHANDLER, CHANDLER

57
00:02:26,187 --> 00:02:27,773
YOU KNOW WHAT
WE SHOULD DO?

58
00:02:27,773 --> 00:02:31,568
YOU AND I SHOULD GO OUT
AND GET SOME NEW SUNGLASSES.

59
00:02:31,568 --> 00:02:33,988
WHAT? NO.
I WANT TO WATCH THIS.

60
00:02:36,657 --> 00:02:37,866
DID YOUR CABLE GO OUT?

61
00:02:37,866 --> 00:02:40,869
NO, NO. THAT'S VH1. YEAH.

62
00:02:40,869 --> 00:02:43,789
I GOT TO TELL YOU, THE MUSIC
THESE KIDS LISTEN TO TODAY

63
00:02:43,789 --> 00:02:45,373
IT'S LIKE A LOT OF NOISE
TO ME. I DON'T KNOW.

64
00:02:47,918 --> 00:02:49,711
JOEY, WHY IS YOUR CABLE OUT?
UH...

65
00:02:49,711 --> 00:02:53,298
OH, BECAUSE
I HAVEN'T REALLY
PAID THE BILL.

66
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:55,592
LOOK, IF YOU NEED MONEY
WOULD YOU PLEASE, PLEASE

67
00:02:55,592 --> 00:02:57,511
JUST LET ME LOAN YOU
SOME MONEY?
NO, CHANDLER.

68
00:02:57,511 --> 00:02:58,929
LOOK, FORGET ABOUT IT, OKAY?

69
00:02:58,929 --> 00:03:01,180
LOOK, I KNOW THINGS HAVE
BEEN A LITTLE TIGHT

70
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:03,767
SINCE JANINE MOVED OUT--
GOD, WAS SHE HOT.

71
00:03:03,767 --> 00:03:05,560
WHOA-HO.
I KNOW.

72
00:03:05,560 --> 00:03:07,688
BUT LOOK, I CAN
HANDLE IT, ALL RIGHT?

73
00:03:07,688 --> 00:03:09,857
I CAN... LISTEN
TO THE RADIO, HUH?

74
00:03:09,857 --> 00:03:13,986
AND, UH, HEY, ROSS GAVE
ME THIS GREAT BOOK.

75
00:03:13,986 --> 00:03:16,195
OKAY, FINE. YOU WANT TO SEE
IF THE JOKE STEALER

76
00:03:16,195 --> 00:03:17,781
WILL LET US WATCH THE SHOW
AT HIS PLACE?

77
00:03:17,781 --> 00:03:18,866
SURE. YEAH.

78
00:03:21,035 --> 00:03:22,744
PAID YOUR PHONE BILL?
NOT SO MUCH.

79
00:03:30,836 --> 00:03:32,754
HEY.

80
00:03:32,754 --> 00:03:33,714
IT'S ONLY YOU.

81
00:03:34,965 --> 00:03:36,215
WH-WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

82
00:03:36,215 --> 00:03:38,093
WE ARE LOOKING
AT A PLAYBOY.

83
00:03:38,093 --> 00:03:39,344
OH, I WANT TO LOOK, TOO.

84
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:45,517
YIKES!
( laughs )

85
00:03:45,517 --> 00:03:46,810
SO DO YOU THINK
THAT THESE PICTURES...

86
00:03:46,810 --> 00:03:48,979
ARE THEY TRYING
TO TELL A STORY?

87
00:03:48,979 --> 00:03:50,438
OH, WELL, YEAH, SURE.

88
00:03:50,438 --> 00:03:52,399
I MEAN, LIKE IN THE CASE
OF THIS YOUNG WOMAN

89
00:03:52,399 --> 00:03:54,860
SHE HAS LOST HER
CLOTHES, SO...

90
00:03:54,860 --> 00:03:57,445
SO SHE RIDES NAKED ON THE
HORSE, SHE'S CRYING OUT

91
00:03:57,445 --> 00:04:01,033
"WHERE ARE THEY?
WHERE ARE THEY?"

92
00:04:01,033 --> 00:04:02,201
WELL, SHE'S NOT GOING
TO FIND THEM

93
00:04:02,201 --> 00:04:03,493
LYING IN THE GRASS
LIKE THAT.

94
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:04,828
( laughing )

95
00:04:04,828 --> 00:04:06,788
GOD...

96
00:04:06,788 --> 00:04:09,083
OH... YEAH.

97
00:04:09,083 --> 00:04:10,250
OH, REMEMBER THE DAYS

98
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,626
WHEN YOU USED TO GO OUT
TO THE BARN

99
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:13,087
LIFT UP YOUR SHIRT
AND BEND OVER?

100
00:04:13,087 --> 00:04:14,379
YEAH.

101
00:04:18,175 --> 00:04:19,384
YOU SEE, NOW...

102
00:04:19,384 --> 00:04:21,803
SEE, NOW, I WOULD
DATE THIS GIRL.

103
00:04:21,803 --> 00:04:24,305
SHE'S CUTE;
SHE'S OUTDOORSY.

104
00:04:24,305 --> 00:04:25,766
YOU KNOW, AND SHE KNOWS
HOW TO BUILD A FIRE.

105
00:04:25,766 --> 00:04:28,060
I MEAN, THAT'S GOT
TO COME IN HANDY.

106
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:29,770
HEY, I GOT A QUESTION.
MM-HMM?

107
00:04:29,770 --> 00:04:34,108
IF YOU HAD TO PICK ONE OF US
TO DATE, WHO WOULD IT BE?

108
00:04:34,108 --> 00:04:35,442
I DON'T KNOW.

109
00:04:35,442 --> 00:04:36,735
ME, NEITHER.
RACHEL.

110
00:04:38,403 --> 00:04:39,738
WHAT?

111
00:04:41,115 --> 00:04:43,700
I DON'T KNOW.

112
00:04:43,700 --> 00:04:45,368
ME, NEITHER.

113
00:04:48,914 --> 00:04:52,000
YOU KNOW, YOU FORGET
HOW MANY GREAT SONGS HEART HAD.

114
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,836
YEAH.
YEAH.

115
00:04:54,836 --> 00:04:59,716
YOU KNOW, "BARRACUDA" WAS
THE FIRST SONG I LEARNED
TO PLAY ON THE KEYBOARD.

116
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:02,719
SO YOU HEARD IT,
YOU REPEATED IT...

117
00:05:02,719 --> 00:05:05,597
SO THAT MUST MEAN...
YOU WROTE IT.

118
00:05:07,348 --> 00:05:09,434
OH, YOU GUYS WITH THIS JOKE.

119
00:05:09,434 --> 00:05:11,311
LOOK, I GOT TO SAY,
I KNOW I CRACKED UP

120
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:13,772
BUT I'M NOT EVEN SURE I GOT IT.

121
00:05:13,772 --> 00:05:15,774
WHAT?

122
00:05:15,774 --> 00:05:17,192
YOU DIDN'T GET IT?

123
00:05:17,192 --> 00:05:19,527
THE DOCTOR IS A MONKEY.

124
00:05:19,527 --> 00:05:21,029
( both laughing )

125
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:23,698
AND MONKEYS CAN'T
WRITE OUT PRESCRIPTIONS.

126
00:05:23,698 --> 00:05:26,118
( both laughing )

127
00:05:26,118 --> 00:05:29,704
YOU ARE NOT ALLOWED
TO LAUGH AT MY JOKE.

128
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:31,248
YOUR JOKE?

129
00:05:31,248 --> 00:05:34,334
WELL, I THINK THE
HEF WOULD DISAGREE

130
00:05:34,334 --> 00:05:39,338
WHICH IS WHY HE SENT
ME A CHECK FOR $100.

131
00:05:39,338 --> 00:05:42,259
SO YOU STOLE MY JOKE,
AND YOU STOLE MY MONEY?

132
00:05:42,259 --> 00:05:45,053
YOU KNOW... I WAS GOING TO
STICK IT IN THE ATM

133
00:05:45,053 --> 00:05:48,223
BUT NOW I THINK I'LL
SHOW THE SEXY TELLER

134
00:05:48,223 --> 00:05:51,018
THAT I AM A PUBLISHED WRITER.

135
00:05:51,018 --> 00:05:54,104
WELL, SHE IS GOING TO KNOW
THAT YOU STOLE THE JOKE.

136
00:05:54,104 --> 00:05:56,231
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO,
FOLLOW ME DOWN THERE?
YEAH.

137
00:05:56,231 --> 00:05:58,900
WELL, I'M NOT GOING
TO GO NOW ANYWAY.
OKAY.

138
00:06:01,653 --> 00:06:03,864
HERE YOU GO.
OH.

139
00:06:03,864 --> 00:06:05,699
UH...

140
00:06:05,699 --> 00:06:07,701
UH, GUNTHER...

141
00:06:07,701 --> 00:06:08,869
I CAN'T PAY FOR
THIS RIGHT NOW

142
00:06:08,869 --> 00:06:10,954
'CAUSE, UH,
I'M NOT WORKING

143
00:06:10,954 --> 00:06:13,665
SO I'VE HAD TO CUT DOWN ON
SOME LUXURIES LIKE, UH...

144
00:06:13,665 --> 00:06:15,458
PAYING FOR STUFF, SO...

145
00:06:17,585 --> 00:06:20,630
WELL... IF YOU WANT,
YOU CAN WORK HERE.

146
00:06:20,630 --> 00:06:23,800
UH, I DON'T KNOW.
IT'S, UH, IT'S JUST...

147
00:06:23,800 --> 00:06:27,304
SEE, I WAS A REGULAR
ON A SOAP OPERA, YOU KNOW...

148
00:06:27,304 --> 00:06:30,557
AND TO GO FROM THAT TO THIS,
IT'S JUST...

149
00:06:30,557 --> 00:06:33,643
AND PLUS, YOU KNOW, I'D HAVE
TO WAIT ON ALL MY FRIENDS.

150
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:35,436
OKAY, BUT THE MONEY'S GOOD.

151
00:06:35,436 --> 00:06:38,815
PLUS YOU GET TO STARE AT RACHEL
AS MUCH AS YOU WANT.

152
00:06:40,942 --> 00:06:42,401
WHAT?

153
00:06:42,401 --> 00:06:43,570
FLEXIBLE HOURS.

154
00:06:43,570 --> 00:06:45,864
OH.

155
00:06:45,864 --> 00:06:47,908
MAYBE I COULD
BE A WAITER.

156
00:06:47,908 --> 00:06:49,408
COULD I USE THE PHONE?

157
00:06:56,499 --> 00:06:58,085
SHE PICKED RACHEL.

158
00:06:58,085 --> 00:06:59,794
I MEAN, SHE TRIED
TO BACK OUT OF IT

159
00:06:59,794 --> 00:07:03,173
BUT IT WAS OBVIOUS--
SHE PICKED RACHEL.

160
00:07:03,173 --> 00:07:06,885
HE TOOK MY JOKE;
HE J-JUST TOOK IT.

161
00:07:06,885 --> 00:07:07,969
THAT'S WRONG.

162
00:07:07,969 --> 00:07:09,512
YOU KNOW WHAT ELSE
IS WRONG?

163
00:07:09,512 --> 00:07:11,472
PHOEBE PICKING RACHEL.

164
00:07:11,472 --> 00:07:13,183
YOU KNOW WHO ELSE
PICKED RACHEL?

165
00:07:13,183 --> 00:07:14,601
ROSS. YOU KNOW
WHAT ELSE ROSS DID?

166
00:07:14,601 --> 00:07:18,105
HE STOLE MY JOKE.

167
00:07:18,105 --> 00:07:20,565
YOU KNOW WHAT? I'M
GOING TO GET A JOKE
JOURNAL, YOU KNOW?

168
00:07:20,565 --> 00:07:22,317
AND DOCUMENT THE
DATE AND TIME

169
00:07:22,317 --> 00:07:24,194
OF EVERY SINGLE
ONE OF MY JOKES.

170
00:07:24,194 --> 00:07:25,946
THAT'S A GOOD IDEA.
YEAH.

171
00:07:25,946 --> 00:07:27,739
YOU KNOW WHAT'S
A BAD IDEA?
PICKING RACHEL.

172
00:07:27,739 --> 00:07:29,241
THAT'S RIGHT.

173
00:07:32,035 --> 00:07:33,578
DID YOU HEAR SOMETHING?

174
00:07:33,578 --> 00:07:35,205
WELL, MAYBE IT'S
THE SOUND OF ROSS

175
00:07:35,205 --> 00:07:38,457
CLIMBING INTO MY BRAIN
AND STEALING MY THOUGHTS.

176
00:07:38,457 --> 00:07:40,501
I THINK IT'S COMING
FROM THE LIVING ROOM.

177
00:07:47,008 --> 00:07:48,385
I FINISHED MY BOOK.

178
00:07:53,974 --> 00:07:55,767
( knocking on door )

179
00:07:55,767 --> 00:07:56,768
HEY, YOU GUYS.

180
00:07:56,768 --> 00:07:58,477
HEY.
HEY.

181
00:07:58,477 --> 00:08:01,106
OH, DON'T YOU GUYS LOOK CUTE.

182
00:08:01,106 --> 00:08:03,066
YOU GUYS MAKE
SUCH A CUTE COUPLE.

183
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:06,527
MONICA, WHAT ARE YOU DOING?

184
00:08:06,527 --> 00:08:08,863
NOTHING. I'M JUST TRYING
TO RECREATE SOME OF THE FUN

185
00:08:08,863 --> 00:08:10,573
THAT WE HAD AT MY PLACE
THE OTHER DAY.

186
00:08:10,573 --> 00:08:12,867
REMEMBER? WHEN YOU PICKED RACHEL
OVER ME?

187
00:08:12,867 --> 00:08:15,662
( laughing ):
THAT WAS FUNNY.

188
00:08:15,662 --> 00:08:17,289
YES, IT WAS KIND OF FUNNY.

189
00:08:17,289 --> 00:08:18,665
IT WASN'T FUNNY AT ALL.

190
00:08:19,874 --> 00:08:21,876
WHY WOULD YOU DO THAT?

191
00:08:21,876 --> 00:08:24,129
WHY DIDN'T YOU PICK ME?

192
00:08:24,129 --> 00:08:25,380
FINE.

193
00:08:25,380 --> 00:08:27,590
THE REASON THAT I WAS LEANING

194
00:08:27,590 --> 00:08:29,843
A LITTLE BIT MORE
TOWARD RACHEL THAN YOU

195
00:08:29,843 --> 00:08:33,554
IS JUST, YOU KNOW, YOU'RE...
KIND OF HIGH MAINTENANCE.

196
00:08:33,554 --> 00:08:35,556
OKAY, LET'S GO TO LUNCH.

197
00:08:35,556 --> 00:08:37,516
THAT... THAT IS
COMPLETELY UNTRUE.

198
00:08:37,516 --> 00:08:39,394
YOU THINK
I'M HIGH MAINTENANCE?

199
00:08:39,394 --> 00:08:41,104
OKAY, PROVE IT--
I WANT YOU TO WRITE OUT A LIST

200
00:08:41,104 --> 00:08:43,315
AND WE'RE GOING TO GO THROUGH IT
POINT BY POINT.

201
00:08:45,775 --> 00:08:49,363
NO, YOU'RE RIGHT--
YOU'RE EASYGOING.

202
00:08:49,363 --> 00:08:51,865
YOU'RE JUST NOT
AS EASYGOING AS RACHEL.

203
00:08:51,865 --> 00:08:54,284
YOU KNOW, SHE'S JUST
MORE... FLEXIBLE

204
00:08:54,284 --> 00:08:56,161
AND-AND MELLOW, THAT'S ALL.

205
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:03,543
WELL, PEOPLE ARE DIFFERENT.
YEAH, YOU KNOW, RACHEL--

206
00:09:03,543 --> 00:09:05,086
SHE'LL DO WHATEVER YOU WANT,
YOU KNOW?

207
00:09:05,086 --> 00:09:07,588
YOU CAN JUST WALK ALL OVER HER.

208
00:09:07,588 --> 00:09:08,923
WHAT? WAIT A MINUTE.

209
00:09:08,923 --> 00:09:10,384
WHAT, ARE YOU SAYING
I'M A PUSHOVER?

210
00:09:10,384 --> 00:09:12,010
I'M NOT A PUSHOVER.

211
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:14,554
OH, OKAY.
YOU'RE NOT A PUSHOVER.

212
00:09:16,764 --> 00:09:18,725
OH, MY... YOU THINK
I'M A PUSHOVER.

213
00:09:18,725 --> 00:09:20,435
WELL, WATCH THIS.
YOU KNOW WHAT?

214
00:09:20,435 --> 00:09:22,979
YOU'RE NOT INVITED TO LUNCH.
WHAT DO YOU THINK OF THAT?

215
00:09:22,979 --> 00:09:24,772
I THINK THAT'S PRETTY
STRONG, IS WHAT I THINK.

216
00:09:24,772 --> 00:09:26,774
COME ON, MONICA,
LET'S GO TO LUNCH.

217
00:09:28,985 --> 00:09:30,611
YOU START WORKING
ON THAT LIST!

218
00:09:33,114 --> 00:09:35,283
I CANNOT BELIEVE HER.
I KNOW.

219
00:09:35,283 --> 00:09:36,659
WHERE DO YOU WANT
TO GO EAT?

220
00:09:36,659 --> 00:09:39,871
OH... OH!
I LOVE THAT JAPANESE PLACE.

221
00:09:39,871 --> 00:09:41,622
I'M SICK OF JAPANESE.
WE'RE NOT GOING THERE.

222
00:09:41,622 --> 00:09:44,959
ALL RIGHT, WELL, WHEREVER
YOU WANT TO GO IS COOL.

223
00:09:49,381 --> 00:09:50,840
OH, HEY, GUNTHER

224
00:09:50,840 --> 00:09:53,843
CHECK THIS OUT.

225
00:09:53,843 --> 00:09:54,969
( laughing )

226
00:09:54,969 --> 00:09:57,972
YEAH, THAT CHANDLER
CRACKS ME UP.

227
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:03,770
HEY, ROSS, LISTEN,
YOU WANT ANYTHING TO DRINK?

228
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:05,021
'CAUSE I'M HEADING UP THERE.

229
00:10:05,021 --> 00:10:06,814
UH, YEAH, I'LL
TAKE A COFFEE.

230
00:10:06,814 --> 00:10:07,815
THANKS, MAN.
SURE.

231
00:10:07,815 --> 00:10:09,234
COFFEE?
NO.

232
00:10:09,234 --> 00:10:10,860
COFFEE? 'CAUSE
I'M GOING UP THERE.

233
00:10:10,860 --> 00:10:13,863
OH, NO, THANK YOU.
OKAY.

234
00:10:13,863 --> 00:10:16,741
YOU GUYS NEED ANYTHING?
'CAUSE I'M HEADING UP THERE.

235
00:10:16,741 --> 00:10:18,118
I'D LOVE A... ICE WATER.

236
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:21,246
( chuckling ):
YOU GOT IT.

237
00:10:21,246 --> 00:10:22,705
JOEY... WHAT
ARE YOU DOING?

238
00:10:22,705 --> 00:10:24,207
( chuckling ):
JUST BEING FRIENDLY.

239
00:10:26,460 --> 00:10:29,254
JOEY, I-I DON'T THINK YOU'RE
SUPPOSED TO GO BACK THERE.

240
00:10:29,254 --> 00:10:30,589
NO, NO, IT'S OKAY.
RIGHT GUNTHER?

241
00:10:32,340 --> 00:10:35,469
DON'T WINK AT ME.

242
00:10:35,469 --> 00:10:36,511
AND PUT ON YOUR APRON.

243
00:10:38,972 --> 00:10:40,723
( chuckling ):
OKAY.

244
00:10:40,723 --> 00:10:42,517
I DON'T SEE YOU ASKING
ANY OTHER PAYING CUSTOMERS

245
00:10:42,517 --> 00:10:45,686
TO PUT ON APRONS.

246
00:10:45,686 --> 00:10:47,688
JOEY... DO YOU WORK HERE?

247
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:48,648
NO.

248
00:10:48,648 --> 00:10:50,233
WAITER?
YEAH?

249
00:10:56,739 --> 00:10:58,116
JOEY, WHAT'S GOING ON?

250
00:10:58,116 --> 00:10:59,742
WHY DIDN'T YOU TELL
US YOU WORK HERE?

251
00:10:59,742 --> 00:11:01,536
WELL...

252
00:11:01,536 --> 00:11:04,414
WELL... IT'S KIND OF
EMBARRASSING, YOU KNOW?

253
00:11:04,414 --> 00:11:07,375
I MEAN, I WAS AN ACTOR;
NOW I'M A WAITER.

254
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:10,462
IT'S SUPPOSED TO GO
IN THE OTHER DIRECTION.

255
00:11:10,462 --> 00:11:12,589
SO IS YOUR APRON--
YOU'RE WEARING IT LIKE A CAPE.

256
00:11:14,549 --> 00:11:17,218
I MEAN, THE JOB'S EASY,
AND THE MONEY'S GOOD, YOU KNOW

257
00:11:17,218 --> 00:11:19,887
AND I GUESS IF I'M GOING
TO BE HANGING OUT HERE ANYWAY

258
00:11:19,887 --> 00:11:22,098
I MIGHT AS WELL GET PAID
FOR IT, RIGHT?

259
00:11:22,098 --> 00:11:25,435
I JUST FEEL KIND OF WEIRD
SERVING YOU GUYS, YOU KNOW?

260
00:11:25,435 --> 00:11:26,436
IT'LL BE GREAT.
OH...

261
00:11:26,436 --> 00:11:27,812
JOEY, COME ON,
I DID IT

262
00:11:27,812 --> 00:11:29,189
AND IT WAS FINE.

263
00:11:29,189 --> 00:11:31,358
YEAH. WHY WOULD IT BE WEIRD?

264
00:11:31,358 --> 00:11:35,612
HEY, JOEY, UH,
COULD I GET SOME COFFEE?

265
00:11:35,612 --> 00:11:37,947
OKAY, I GUESS IT DOESN'T
SEEM THAT WEIRD.

266
00:11:37,947 --> 00:11:40,534
SERIOUSLY, I ASKED YOU BEFORE--
YOU STILL HAVEN'T GOTTEN IT.

267
00:11:42,243 --> 00:11:44,538
SEE, NOW IT'S WEIRD AGAIN.

268
00:11:44,538 --> 00:11:46,456
I THINK IT'S GREAT
THAT YOU WORK HERE.

269
00:11:46,456 --> 00:11:48,625
YOU'RE GONNA MAKE A LOT OF
MONEY AND HERE'S YOUR FIRST TIP:

270
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,419
DON'T EAT YELLOW SNOW.

271
00:11:51,419 --> 00:11:54,464
( chuckling )

272
00:11:54,464 --> 00:11:56,715
2:15. COFFEE HOUSE.

273
00:11:58,468 --> 00:12:00,554
WELL, YOU KNOW, THIS IS GREAT--
FINALLY, I HAVE SOMEONE

274
00:12:00,554 --> 00:12:02,430
I CAN PASS ON MY WISDOM TO.

275
00:12:02,430 --> 00:12:04,182
LET ME TELL YOU
ABOUT A COUPLE THINGS I LEARNED

276
00:12:04,182 --> 00:12:05,808
WHILE WORKING
AT THE COFFEE HOUSE.

277
00:12:05,808 --> 00:12:09,646
UM, FIRST OF ALL, THE
CUSTOMER IS ALWAYS RIGHT;

278
00:12:09,646 --> 00:12:12,649
A SMILE GOES A LONG WAY;

279
00:12:14,108 --> 00:12:16,277
AND IF ANYONE
IS EVER RUDE TO YOU...

280
00:12:16,277 --> 00:12:18,029
SNEEZE MUFFIN.

281
00:12:19,989 --> 00:12:22,158
THANKS, RACH.

282
00:12:22,158 --> 00:12:25,537
HEY, LOOK, YOU GUYS
ARE JUST TERRIFIC, YOU KNOW?

283
00:12:25,537 --> 00:12:26,871
NOW, HOW ABOUT
CLEARING OUT OF HERE

284
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:29,207
SO I CAN GET
SOME NEW CUSTOMERS, HUH?

285
00:12:29,207 --> 00:12:30,500
IT'S ALL ABOUT TURNOVER.

286
00:12:30,500 --> 00:12:32,419
( laughs )

287
00:12:32,419 --> 00:12:34,546
JOEY...

288
00:12:34,546 --> 00:12:37,340
SERIOUSLY,
CAN I GET MY COFFEE?

289
00:12:37,340 --> 00:12:38,550
OH, I'M SORRY, ROSS.

290
00:12:38,550 --> 00:12:40,343
I'LL GET IT FOR
YOU RIGHT NOW.

291
00:12:40,343 --> 00:12:43,221
AND SINCE I MADE YOU WAIT,
I'LL TOSS IN A FREE MUFFIN.

292
00:12:49,644 --> 00:12:52,313
PHOEBE, WE WOULD LIKE
TO TALK TO YOU FOR A SECOND.

293
00:12:52,313 --> 00:12:53,940
OKAY.

294
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:55,275
SO...

295
00:12:55,275 --> 00:12:57,235
MAYBE I AM A LITTLE
HIGH MAINTENANCE

296
00:12:57,235 --> 00:13:00,363
AND MAYBE RACHEL IS
A LITTLE BIT OF A PUSHOVER

297
00:13:00,363 --> 00:13:02,240
BUT YOU KNOW WHAT
WE DECIDED THAT YOU ARE?

298
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:03,908
YES, WE ARE VERY SORRY
TO TELL YOU THIS

299
00:13:03,908 --> 00:13:06,327
BUT YOU, PHOEBE, ARE FLAKY.

300
00:13:06,327 --> 00:13:07,537
HA!

301
00:13:09,414 --> 00:13:12,626
THAT'S TRUE.
I AM FLAKY.

302
00:13:12,626 --> 00:13:13,918
SO, WHAT?
YOU'RE JUST, UH,

303
00:13:13,918 --> 00:13:16,588
YOU'RE JUST OKAY
WITH BEING FLAKY?

304
00:13:16,588 --> 00:13:19,090
YEAH, TOTALLY.

305
00:13:19,090 --> 00:13:21,676
WELL, THEN I'M OKAY
WITH BEING HIGH MAINTENANCE.

306
00:13:21,676 --> 00:13:24,803
YEAH, AND I AM OKAY
WITH BEING A PUSHOVER.

307
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:25,804
THAT'S GREAT.

308
00:13:25,804 --> 00:13:27,848
GOOD FOR YOU GUYS!

309
00:13:27,848 --> 00:13:29,392
I AM NOT HIGH MAINTENANCE!

310
00:13:29,392 --> 00:13:30,893
AND I AM NOT
A PUSHOVER!

311
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:33,647
WHO SAID YOU WERE?!

312
00:13:33,647 --> 00:13:34,689
YOU DID!
YOU DID!

313
00:13:34,689 --> 00:13:35,690
I'M FLAKY.

314
00:13:35,690 --> 00:13:37,233
I'LL SAY ANYTHING.

315
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:45,950
HEY, GUNTHER,
CAN YOU COVER FOR ME?

316
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:47,577
I JUST GOT AN AUDITION.

317
00:13:47,577 --> 00:13:50,079
NO, I'M LEAVING
TO GET MY HAIR DYED.

318
00:13:51,748 --> 00:13:53,792
REALLY? I LIKE
YOUR NATURAL COLOR.

319
00:13:56,043 --> 00:13:58,045
COME ON, IT'S
A GREAT PART.

320
00:13:58,045 --> 00:13:59,922
I'M THE LEAD GUY'S
BEST FRIEND

321
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:01,800
AND I WAIT FOR HIM
IN THIS BAR AND SAVE HIS SEAT.

322
00:14:01,800 --> 00:14:03,176
LISTEN. LISTEN.

323
00:14:03,176 --> 00:14:05,052
I'M SORRY. THAT SEAT'S SAVED.

324
00:14:07,221 --> 00:14:08,807
THAT'S THE WHOLE PART?

325
00:14:08,807 --> 00:14:12,352
OKAY, MAYBE HE'S NOT
HIS BEST FRIEND, BUT...

326
00:14:12,352 --> 00:14:13,436
OKAY, I'LL SEE YOU
IN AN HOUR.

327
00:14:16,648 --> 00:14:18,650
I COULD TOTALLY
GET THAT PART.

328
00:14:18,650 --> 00:14:20,401
I'M SORRY,
THIS SEAT IS TAKEN.

329
00:14:20,401 --> 00:14:23,488
OH, EXCUSE ME.
NO, NO, NO, I...
I DIDN'T MEAN YOU

330
00:14:23,488 --> 00:14:26,073
BUT, UH, YOU BELIEVE ME, HUH?

331
00:14:26,073 --> 00:14:30,119
I BELIEVED YOU WERE SAVING
THIS SEAT FOR SOMEONE.

332
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:31,788
SO YOU'D HIRE ME, RIGHT?

333
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:35,082
FOR WHAT?

334
00:14:35,082 --> 00:14:36,376
EXACTLY!
ALL RIGHT, UH,

335
00:14:36,376 --> 00:14:38,795
EVERYBODY, LISTEN UP.
THE COFFEEHOUSE

336
00:14:38,795 --> 00:14:40,797
IS GOING TO BE
CLOSED FOR ABOUT AN HOUR.

337
00:14:40,797 --> 00:14:41,798
All:
WHAT?!

338
00:14:41,798 --> 00:14:43,424
WE JUST
GOT HERE.

339
00:14:43,424 --> 00:14:45,176
YEAH, IT'S, UH,
IT'S FOR THE KIDS.

340
00:14:45,176 --> 00:14:48,262
YEAH, TO, UH,
KEEP THE KIDS OFF DRUGS.

341
00:14:48,262 --> 00:14:52,475
YUP, IT'S A VERY IMPORTANT ISSUE
IN THIS MONTH'S PLAYBOY.

342
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:54,185
I'M SURE YOU ALL READ ABOUT IT.

343
00:14:54,185 --> 00:14:55,854
THERE YOU GO.

344
00:15:04,654 --> 00:15:06,698
IT'S MY JOKE.
IT'S MY JOKE.

345
00:15:09,826 --> 00:15:13,079
IT'S MY JOKE.
IT'S MY JOKE.

346
00:15:13,079 --> 00:15:15,790
YOU KNOW, I DON'T
THINK WE'RE GOING
TO SETTLE THIS.

347
00:15:15,790 --> 00:15:17,584
NO. LET'S HAVE
MONICA DECIDE.

348
00:15:17,584 --> 00:15:18,626
YEAH.

349
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:19,711
YEAH.
HEY, MON!

350
00:15:19,711 --> 00:15:21,629
MON, GET OUT HERE!
MONICA!

351
00:15:21,629 --> 00:15:23,005
OKAY, OKAY.

352
00:15:23,005 --> 00:15:25,049
YOU HAVE TO HELP US
DECIDE WHOSE JOKE THIS IS.

353
00:15:25,049 --> 00:15:26,551
WHY DO I HAVE
TO DECIDE?

354
00:15:26,551 --> 00:15:29,387
BECAUSE YOU'RE
THE ONLY ONE
THAT CAN BE FAIR.

355
00:15:29,387 --> 00:15:31,305
I CAN'T BE FAIR.
YOU'RE MY BOYFRIEND.

356
00:15:31,305 --> 00:15:33,767
YEAH, BUT I'M YOUR BROTHER.
WE'RE FAMILY.

357
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:37,729
THAT'S THE MOST IMPORTANT THING
IN THE WORLD.

358
00:15:39,564 --> 00:15:41,858
DON'T TRY TO SWAY HER.

359
00:15:41,858 --> 00:15:44,736
I'M YOUR ONLY CHANCE
TO HAVE A BABY.

360
00:15:47,947 --> 00:15:49,449
OKAY, LET'S GO.

361
00:15:49,449 --> 00:15:52,535
ALL RIGHT, UM, OKAY,
WE'LL EACH TELL YOU

362
00:15:52,535 --> 00:15:53,787
HOW WE CAME UP
WITH THE JOKE

363
00:15:53,787 --> 00:15:55,747
AND THEN YOU DECIDE
WHICH ONE OF US

364
00:15:55,747 --> 00:15:58,958
IS TELLING THE TRUTH-- ME.

365
00:15:58,958 --> 00:15:59,959
CHANDLER, YOU GO FIRST.

366
00:15:59,959 --> 00:16:01,294
OKAY, I THOUGHT
OF THE JOKE

367
00:16:01,294 --> 00:16:03,838
TWO MONTHS AGO
AT LUNCH WITH STEVE.

368
00:16:03,838 --> 00:16:05,339
IS HE THE GUY
I MET AT CHRISTMAS?

369
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:06,549
CAN I FINISH MY STORY?

370
00:16:06,549 --> 00:16:09,427
DO YOU WANT ME TO PICK YOU?

371
00:16:09,427 --> 00:16:12,639
SEE, I WOULD NEVER
SNAP AT YOU LIKE THAT.

372
00:16:20,187 --> 00:16:21,564
CONTINUE.

373
00:16:21,564 --> 00:16:24,358
OKAY, SO STEVE SAID
HE HAD TO GO TO THE DOCTOR

374
00:16:24,358 --> 00:16:27,278
AND STEVE'S DOCTOR'S NAME
IS DR. MOMPEY.

375
00:16:27,278 --> 00:16:29,405
SO I SAID, "DR. MONKEY?"

376
00:16:29,405 --> 00:16:32,492
AND THAT IS HOW THE WHOLE
DR. MONKEY THING CAME UP.

377
00:16:36,621 --> 00:16:39,081
ARE YOU KIDDING?

378
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:41,709
OKAY, LOOK, I STUDY
EVOLUTION.

379
00:16:41,709 --> 00:16:43,377
REMEMBER? EVOLUTION?

380
00:16:43,377 --> 00:16:45,171
MONKEY INTO MAN.

381
00:16:45,171 --> 00:16:46,297
PLUS, I'M A DOCTOR

382
00:16:46,297 --> 00:16:49,383
AND I HAD A MONKEY.

383
00:16:52,178 --> 00:16:54,263
I'M DR. MONKEY!

384
00:16:56,975 --> 00:16:59,686
I'M NOT ARGUING
WITH THAT.

385
00:16:59,686 --> 00:17:01,855
I'VE HEARD ENOUGH.
I HAVE MADE MY DECISION.

386
00:17:01,855 --> 00:17:03,857
( both grunting )

387
00:17:03,857 --> 00:17:07,318
YOU ARE BOTH IDIOTS.

388
00:17:07,318 --> 00:17:10,363
THE JOKE IS NOT FUNNY
AND IT'S OFFENSIVE TO WOMEN,

389
00:17:10,363 --> 00:17:14,158
AND DOCTORS, AND MONKEYS.

390
00:17:14,158 --> 00:17:16,327
YOU SHOULDN'T BE ARGUING
OVER WHO GETS CREDIT

391
00:17:16,327 --> 00:17:18,496
YOU SHOULD BE ARGUING
OVER WHO GETS BLAMED

392
00:17:18,496 --> 00:17:21,499
FOR INFLICTING THIS HORRIBLE
JOKE UPON THE WORLD.

393
00:17:21,499 --> 00:17:22,959
NOW, LET IT GO.

394
00:17:22,959 --> 00:17:25,252
THE JOKE SUCKS!

395
00:17:30,675 --> 00:17:31,676
IT'S YOUR JOKE.

396
00:17:31,676 --> 00:17:32,886
IT IS NOT.

397
00:17:48,317 --> 00:17:49,944
MY GOD, CHANDLER,
THERE YOU ARE.

398
00:17:49,944 --> 00:17:52,363
HI-I!

399
00:17:52,363 --> 00:17:54,782
HEY, IT'S PHOEBE
AND RACHEL.

400
00:17:54,782 --> 00:17:55,867
WHY DON'T YOU
TELL THEM

401
00:17:55,867 --> 00:17:57,035
WHAT YOU WERE
TELLING ME EARLIER

402
00:17:57,035 --> 00:17:59,871
ABOUT ME NOT BEING
HIGH MAINTENANCE.

403
00:18:02,164 --> 00:18:08,087
MONICA IS A
SELF-SUFFICIENT,
TOGETHER LADY.

404
00:18:08,087 --> 00:18:11,298
BEING WITH HER HAS
BEEN LIKE BEING
ON A VACATION.

405
00:18:13,551 --> 00:18:16,637
AND WHAT MAY
BE PERCEIVED AS
HIGH MAINTENANCE

406
00:18:16,637 --> 00:18:20,516
IS MERELY ATTENTION
TO DETAIL AND...

407
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:21,893
( mumbles )

408
00:18:21,893 --> 00:18:24,186
GENEROSITY
OF SPIRIT.

409
00:18:25,730 --> 00:18:27,648
WOW.
YOU KNOW WHAT?

410
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:30,902
THAT IS THE BEST FAKE SPEECH
I THINK I'VE EVER HEARD.

411
00:18:30,902 --> 00:18:33,780
REALLY? NO, I'VE HEARD BETTER.

412
00:18:33,780 --> 00:18:35,990
WAIT. WAIT. HE CAME UP
WITH THAT HIMSELF.

413
00:18:35,990 --> 00:18:37,575
TELL THEM, CHANDLER.

414
00:18:37,575 --> 00:18:38,993
I'M OUT OF WORDS.

415
00:18:38,993 --> 00:18:40,703
SHOULD I JUST SAY
THE WHOLE THING AGAIN?

416
00:18:40,703 --> 00:18:42,413
I AM NOT HIGH MAINTENANCE.

417
00:18:42,413 --> 00:18:43,414
I AM NOT.

418
00:18:43,414 --> 00:18:44,707
CHANDLER!

419
00:18:47,293 --> 00:18:48,711
YOU'RE A LITTLE
HIGH MAINTENANCE.

420
00:18:48,711 --> 00:18:50,088
( gasps )

421
00:18:50,088 --> 00:18:53,091
YOU ARE ON MY LIST.

422
00:18:53,091 --> 00:18:56,844
LOOK, I'M SORRY,
BUT YOU'RE NOT EASYGOING

423
00:18:56,844 --> 00:18:58,596
BUT YOU'RE PASSIONATE

424
00:18:58,596 --> 00:19:00,098
AND THAT'S GOOD.

425
00:19:00,098 --> 00:19:02,224
AND WHEN YOU GET UPSET
ABOUT THE LITTLE THINGS

426
00:19:02,224 --> 00:19:03,559
I THINK THAT I'M PRETTY GOOD

427
00:19:03,559 --> 00:19:05,937
AT MAKING YOU FEEL BETTER
ABOUT THAT.

428
00:19:05,937 --> 00:19:07,396
AND THAT'S GOOD, TOO.

429
00:19:07,396 --> 00:19:09,356
SO THEY CAN SAY
THAT YOU'RE HIGH MAINTENANCE

430
00:19:09,356 --> 00:19:12,652
BUT IT'S OKAY
BECAUSE I LIKE...

431
00:19:13,778 --> 00:19:16,196
MAINTAINING YOU.

432
00:19:23,871 --> 00:19:25,623
I DIDN'T EVEN TELL
HIM TO SAY THAT.

433
00:19:28,084 --> 00:19:29,836
OKAY.

434
00:19:29,836 --> 00:19:30,878
ALL RIGHT, YOU'RE
OFF MY LIST.

435
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:33,047
I'M OFF THE LIST.

436
00:19:33,047 --> 00:19:35,424
PHOEBE...

437
00:19:35,424 --> 00:19:37,468
IT'S OKAY THAT YOU
DON'T WANT ME TO
BE YOUR GIRLFRIEND

438
00:19:37,468 --> 00:19:40,096
BECAUSE I HAVE
THE BEST BOYFRIEND.

439
00:19:42,056 --> 00:19:45,601
YOU KNOW, SUDDENLY
I FIND YOU VERY ATTRACTIVE.

440
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:50,397
HEY, BUDDY BOY,
HOW DID THE AUDITION GO?

441
00:19:50,397 --> 00:19:52,358
OH, NOT GOOD.

442
00:19:52,358 --> 00:19:54,902
I DIDN'T GET THE PART
AND, UH, LOST MY JOB HERE

443
00:19:54,902 --> 00:19:55,945
SO...

444
00:19:55,945 --> 00:19:57,989
WOW, THAT IS A BAD AUDITION.

445
00:19:59,991 --> 00:20:02,827
HOW DID YOU LOSE YOUR JOB HERE?

446
00:20:02,827 --> 00:20:04,411
WELL, I HAD THE AUDITION

447
00:20:04,411 --> 00:20:05,997
BUT GUNTHER SAID I HAD
TO STAY HERE AND BE IN CHARGE

448
00:20:05,997 --> 00:20:08,206
SO HE COULD GO
GET HIS HAIR DYED.

449
00:20:08,206 --> 00:20:10,584
SO, I WENT ANYWAY
AND THEN HE FIRED ME.

450
00:20:10,584 --> 00:20:12,336
HE LEFT WORK
IN THE MIDDLE OF THE DAY

451
00:20:12,336 --> 00:20:15,131
TO DO A PERSONAL ERRAND
AND LEFT YOU IN CHARGE

452
00:20:15,131 --> 00:20:17,216
WHEN YOU'VE BEEN WORKING HERE
FOR TWO DAYS.

453
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:19,135
THAT'S NOT RIGHT.

454
00:20:19,135 --> 00:20:21,179
WHAT ARE YOU GOING TO DO?

455
00:20:21,179 --> 00:20:23,973
WELL, JOEY
YOU CAN'T LET HIM
GET AWAY WITH THAT.

456
00:20:23,973 --> 00:20:25,975
YOU KNOW WHAT? I'M NOT GOING
TO LET HIM GET AWAY WITH THAT.

457
00:20:25,975 --> 00:20:27,601
I'M GOING TO SAY SOMETHING TO...

458
00:20:27,601 --> 00:20:29,227
NO, I REALLY SHOULDN'T
SAY ANYTHING TO HIM.

459
00:20:29,227 --> 00:20:31,939
NO, I SHOULD SAY
SOMETHING TO HIM!

460
00:20:34,025 --> 00:20:37,235
GUNTHER, I WANT
YOU TO GIVE JOEY
HIS JOB BACK.

461
